# Netlify redirects. First match wins, and a real file on disk is served before any
# non-forced rule. There is deliberately NO catch-all: unknown URLs get /404.html with a
# real 404 status, so Google never indexes junk URLs as copies of the homepage (soft 404).
#
# Every public page is now a real file:
#   /                         index.html (homepage SPA)
#   /about/ /contact/ /mortgage-calculator/ /deep-analysis/arina-east-residences/
#                             pre-rendered copies of the SPA with their own head (build-pages.cjs)
#   /project/<slug>/  /new-launch-condos/  /insights/  /insights/<slug>/   (build-pages.cjs)
#   /news/  /undervalued-pty/  /hdb-resale-timeline/   (their own scripts)
# Without a trailing slash Netlify redirects /about -> /about/ automatically.
# A real file is served before a non-forced rule, so the index.html rules are
# forced. Do not add a rule that removes a trailing slash: that loops.

# The Netlify subdomain serves the same files. Send it to the canonical host.
# Internal files are never public (publish dir is "."): build scripts, source data, notes and config
# answer with the real 404 page. Forced (!) so the file on disk is not served. Nothing on the site loads these.
